ian, and Japanese duo. The gold/silver medals by twins was only the second time this had occurred at the Olympics, the other time occurring in 1980 coxless pairs rowing, won by the Landvoigt twins (GDR), with the Pimenov twins (URS) taking silver."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Figures"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/51075"} "Karen Josephson"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/51076"} "Sarah Josephson"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "92.575 (1)"] [:td {} "191.215 (1)"] [:td {} "192.175 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/45888"} "Penny Vilagos"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/45889"} "Vicky Vilagos"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "90.354 (2)"] [:td {} "188.594 (2)"] [:td {} "189.394 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/48683"} "Fumiko Okuno"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/48708"} "Aki Takayama"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "88.468 (3)"] [:td {} "186.068 (3)"] [:td {} "186.868 (3)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/50714"} "Anna Kozlova"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/50039"} "Olga Sedakova"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/cou